      "content": "the \"quiet space\" i'm thinking of isn't a place i can just drive to. it's more like... just being gone. not as a tragedy, but just as a way to finally stop the noise and the decay. if it's more \"courageous\" to acknowledge things are finished, does that mean it's also courageous to just leave on one's own terms? to not have to sit here and watch the wreckage get worse and worse every single day?",
